# Task 7 — 图标量化与正式构建 Report

## Status

**DONE_WITH_CONCERNS:** Unicode-path JSC execution is resolved and the signed production release completes with all mandated flags. The signing pair is local demo material and remains untracked.

## Icon optimization

| Measurement | Baseline | Optimized | Change |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| `src/common/app-icon-512.png` | 390,550 bytes | 22,505 bytes | -368,045 bytes (-94.24%) |

`scripts/optimize-icon.py` reproduces the prescribed 256-color FASTOCTREE/Floyd-Steinberg indexed PNG conversion. The original and temporary output were visually inspected before replacement: transparent corners, the circular edge, waveform mark, and gradients are retained with no visible halo or distracting banding. Pillow verification confirms `512x512`, mode `P`, and PNG transparency.

The output is below the 50–100 KB target (22,505 bytes); the supplied 256-color indexed conversion compresses more efficiently than that range while retaining acceptable visual quality.

## Package measurements

| Artifact | Baseline | Current | Notes |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---|
| Development RPK (`com.openvela.wristrhythm.debug.1.0.0.rpk`) | 415,184 bytes | 49,018 bytes | -366,166 bytes (-88.19%); generated by `npm run build` |
| Release RPK (`com.openvela.wristrhythm.release.1.0.0.rpk`) | not present | 44,880 bytes | generated by staged `npm run build:release` |

## Build evidence

- `npm run build`: exited 0; development options remained `enableJsc: false`, `optimizeCssAttr: false`, `dropConsole: false`, mode `development`.
- `npm run build:release` and `npm run release`: invoke `aiot release --enable-jsc --optimize-css-attr --enable-image-png8 --drop-console true`. Logs report `enableJsc: true`, `optimizeCssAttr: true`, `dropConsole: "true"`, `enableImagePng8: true`, and mode `production`.
- Final command: `npm run build:release` exited 0 and generated the non-empty signed artifact at `F:\\项目\\openvela\\.worktrees\\runtime-optimization\\dist\\com.openvela.wristrhythm.release.1.0.0.rpk` (44,880 bytes). `npm run test` passed 20 logic, 9 runtime, and 4 runner tests.

## Unicode-path resolution and final diagnosis

Direct JSC probes over the same unpacked development package succeed from an ASCII-only path (`C:\\Temp\\openvela-jsc-probe-…`, exit 0) and fail from an otherwise identical Unicode path (`C:\\Temp\\项目-jsc-probe-…`, exit 1, `read_dir: opendir failed: 2 No such file or directory`). The current worktree and AIoT temporary build path contain `项目`.

`scripts/release-runner.js` now stages every non-generated root project input (including `src/`, optional `sign/`, configuration files/directories) and a `node_modules` junction under an ASCII-only system-temp directory. It runs the unchanged native flags, validates a non-empty `.release.*.rpk`, copies that artifact to the real `dist/`, and removes only its exact stage root. It also converts AIoT's logged build errors into a nonzero process exit because the toolkit itself reports exit code 0 on failures.

TDD evidence: `test/release-runner.test.js` first failed with `MODULE_NOT_FOUND` for the absent runner; the initial three tests passed after implementation. A subsequent failure (`runner.hasReleaseFailure is not a function`) preceded the log-failure check; all four focused tests now pass. `npm run test` passes 20 logic, 9 runtime, and 4 runner tests; `npm run build` exits 0.

With the validated local demo signing pair in `sign/release/`, the final staged release passes `Generate jsc bytecode`, packages the signed RPK, copies it back to the real `dist/`, and exits 0. The runner still removes its exact temporary stage root. The pair was not committed and is suitable for local validation only; replace it with managed production signing material for distribution.

